I have to agree with aionys here.  As you correctly point, the CLL says "th=
at
an already-filled place is skipped".  "fi ku" is not "filled", however.  It
is empty.  It's merely mentioned that a slot exists, but it does not fill
it.  Hence "FA KU" are  basically semantically meaningless structures,
unlike FA zo'e

  There are, however, of course, lotsa bugs with jboski (why, oh why, did
genrei have to go?), such as not liking LI structures at the end of an
utterance that are not terminate with lo'o (i.e. "mi mitre li re" will bomb=
)
                  --gejyspa


